      "_et_pb_old_content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It's been a whirlwind couple of weeks. While I worked on preparing <em>When the Stars Conspire </em>for another round of beta reads and sketched the initial shape of <em>Not A Cult, I Promise</em>, I also spoke at my first in-person writing-related event after two years of virtual speaking engagements. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Oh, and I spent some time on the beach for the first time in just as long (if not longer, honestly).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Lakefly Writers Recap</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After originally having been slated to speak at the 2020 iteration of <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://lakeflywriters.org/" target="_blank">Lakefly Writers Conference</a>—which would go on to be canceled in 2020 and 2021 as a result of the pandemic—I was invited to  present at the 2022 installment of this fantastic event in Oshkosh, Wisconsin. Here are some photos from my presentation on the Five Fun Floaties of Scene Structure and from around the conference in general.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:group -->
<div class="wp-block-group"><!-- wp:jetpack/tiled-gallery {"columnWidths":[["20.94844","37.15468","20.94844","20.94844"]],"ids":[10099,10104,10100,10094]} -->
<div class="wp-block-jetpack-tiled-gallery aligncenter is-style-rectangular"><div class="tiled-gallery__gallery"><div class="tiled-gallery__row"><div class="tiled-gallery__col" style="flex-basis:20.94844%"><figure class="tiled-gallery__item"><img alt="Author Ryan R. Campbell stands beside a projected slide that asks, &quot;What's a scene?&quot;" data-height="4032" data-id="10099" data-link="https://ryanrcampbell.com/img_9890/" data-url="https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_9890-768x1024.jpg" data-width="3024" src="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_9890-768x1024.jpg?ssl=1" data-amp-layout="responsive"/></figure></div><div class="tiled-gallery__col" style="flex-basis:37.15468%"><figure class="tiled-gallery__item"><img alt="Ryan R. Campbell holds his book AND AMPERSAND in one hand while standing alongside a projected screen that displays his book SCAMBAIT" data-height="1536" data-id="10104" data-link="https://ryanrcampbell.com/img_6180/" data-url="https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_6180-1024x768.jpg" data-width="2048" src="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_6180-1024x768.jpg?ssl=1" data-amp-layout="responsive"/></figure></div><div class="tiled-gallery__col" style="flex-basis:20.94844%"><figure class="tiled-gallery__item"><img alt="Ryan R. Campbell sits at a table with copies of his books SCAMBAIT and AND AMPERSAND displayed in front of him." data-height="4032" data-id="10100" data-link="https://ryanrcampbell.com/img_9892/" data-url="https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_9892-768x1024.jpg" data-width="3024" src="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_9892-768x1024.jpg?ssl=1" data-amp-layout="responsive"/></figure></div><div class="tiled-gallery__col" style="flex-basis:20.94844%"><figure class="tiled-gallery__item"><img alt="Author Ryan R. Campbell gestures to a room of attendees while starting his presentation on scene structure." data-height="4032" data-id="10094" data-link="https://ryanrcampbell.com/img_9884/" data-url="https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_9884-768x1024.jpg" data-width="3024" src="https://i1.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/IMG_9884-768x1024.jpg?ssl=1" data-amp-layout="responsive"/></figure></div></div></div></div>
<!-- /wp:jetpack/tiled-gallery --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Rolling Around Rincón</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Okay, so we only rolled around Rincón if you count the rental car, but the point is this—my wife and I were able to go on our first vacation since February 2019 in recent weeks as well. This was our second trip together to Puerto Rico, though my wife has been there a number of other times for school and subsequently to visit friends.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

