    "author": 1,
    "categories": [
      571548501,
    ],
    "comment_status": "open",
    "content": {
      "protected": false,
      "rendered": "<p>[et_pb_section fb_built=”1&#8243; _builder_version=”3.22&#8243;][et_pb_row _builder_version=”3.25&#8243; background_size=”initial” background_position=”top_left” background_repeat=”repeat”][et_pb_column type=”4_4&#8243; _builder_version=”3.25&#8243; custom_padding=”|||” custom_padding__hover=”|||”][et_pb_text _builder_version=”3.27.4&#8243; background_size=”initial” background_position=”top_left” background_repeat=”repeat”]<!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>It's never easy, but it can get easier.</p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>At least that seems to be the trend; in the last week alone, I've <strong>completed revisions for the final draft of <em>Scambait</em></strong>, have begun to work on <strong>the back cover copy</strong>, and<strong> </strong>I've initiated <strong>conversations with book cover designers.</strong></p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>And you know what? It feels good. </p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>Sure, I've got my trepidations. So much work lies ahead. There's book formatting, ISBN registration, seeking early readers for the sake of reviews and blurbs—the list goes on.</p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>Through it all, what keeps me going is the thought that <em>Scambait </em>will, at some point this year, be out in the world. <strong>And I really enjoyed reading it again after almost a year away.</strong></p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>Seriously,<strong> I actually laughed out loud a couple of times</strong>, which, if you know me, is a rarity in the world of books. Was I laughing at my own jokes? I guess, yeah, but they felt less like my own jokes than they did like those of the books' characters, which I think is a good sign.</p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:quote {"className":"is-style-large"} --></p>
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-style-large">
<p>… they felt less like my own jokes than they did like those of the books' characters.</p>
<p><cite>- on re-reading <em>Scambait</em> after a year away</cite></p></blockquote>
<p><!-- /divi:quote --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>So, the work continues. I'm hopeful that <strong>two weeks from now I'll have back cover copy to share</strong>, and, optimistically, in 4-6 weeks we'll be ready for a cover reveal.</p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><strong>I'm excited, are you? </strong>Tell me in the comments if you've ever experienced the above—laughing at jokes long forgotten in between reads of a particular book. </p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph --></p>
<p><!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>Or, if you're an author having a similar experience in your own journey to publication, the comment section is waiting for you!</p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph -->[/et_pb_text][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][et_pb_row column_structure=”1_2,1_2&#8243; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” background_color=”rgba(0,0,0,0)” animation_style=”fade” global_module=”9256&#8243;][et_pb_column type=”1_2&#8243; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”][et_pb_image src=”<a href="https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/And-Ampersand-with-Coffee-on-Wood-Table.jpg&#038;#8221">https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/And-Ampersand-with-Coffee-on-Wood-Table.jpg&#038;#8221</a>; title_text=”And Ampersand with Coffee on Wood Table” align=”center” _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” background_color=”rgba(0,0,0,0)” animation_style=”fade”][/et_pb_image][/et_pb_column][et_pb_column type=”1_2&#8243; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”][et_pb_text _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”]</p>
<h2 style="text-align: center;">Now Available</h2>
<p style="text-align: center;"><i>“Reminiscent of Hemingway and De Lillo. I highly recommend this collection.”<br /></i>-Award-Winning Author Ivy Ngeow</p>
<p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_button button_url=”<a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/1736387111&#038;#8243" rel="nofollow">https://www.amazon.com/dp/1736387111&#038;#8243</a>; url_new_window=”on” button_text=”BUY THE BOOK NOW” button_alignment=”center” _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” custom_button=”on” button_text_size=”14px” button_text_color=”#000000&#8243; button_border_radius=”3px” button_letter_spacing=”2px” button_font=”|700|||||||” animation_style=”fold”][/et_pb_button][et_pb_button button_url=”<a href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/56528914-and-ampersand&#038;#8221" rel="nofollow">https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/56528914-and-ampersand&#038;#8221</a>; url_new_window=”on” button_text=”ADD IT ON GOODREADS” button_alignment=”center” _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” custom_button=”on” button_text_size=”14px” button_text_color=”#000000&#8243; button_border_radius=”3px” button_letter_spacing=”2px” button_font=”|700|||||||”][/et_pb_button][et_pb_button button_url=”<a href="https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Glassed-Excerpt-from-And-Ampersand-by-Ryan-R.-Campbell.pdf&#038;#8221">https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Glassed-Excerpt-from-And-Ampersand-by-Ryan-R.-Campbell.pdf&#038;#8221</a>; url_new_window=”on” button_text=”READ AN EXCERPT NOW” button_alignment=”center” _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” custom_button=”on” button_text_size=”14px” button_text_color=”#000000&#8243; button_border_radius=”3px” button_letter_spacing=”2px” button_font=”|700|||||||”][/et_pb_button][et_pb_social_media_follow _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; text_orientation=”center” animation_style=”slide” animation_direction=”top” animation_intensity_slide=”10%”][et_pb_social_media_follow_network social_network=”facebook” url=”<a href="http://www.facebook.com/iamrrcampbell&#038;#8221" rel="nofollow">http://www.facebook.com/iamrrcampbell&#038;#8221</a>; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; background_