    "content": {
      "protected": false,
      "rendered": "<p>[et_pb_section fb_built=”1&#8243; _builder_version=”3.22&#8243;][et_pb_row _builder_version=”3.25&#8243; background_size=”initial” background_position=”top_left” background_repeat=”repeat”][et_pb_column type=”4_4&#8243; _builder_version=”3.25&#8243; custom_padding=”|||” custom_padding__hover=”|||”][et_pb_text _builder_version=”3.27.4&#8243; background_size=”initial” background_position=”top_left” background_repeat=”repeat”]<!-- divi:paragraph --></p>
<p>I recently had the opportunity <a href='https://www.nedaaria.info/post/writer-vs-writer-interview-ryan-r-campbell' rel='noopener noreferrer' target='_blank'>to be interviewed</a> for author Neda Aria's “Writer vs. Writer” series.</p>
<p><span style="font-size: 17px;">In it, I explore what went into </span><em style="font-size: 17px;">And Ampersand</em><span style="font-size: 17px;">, what </span><strong style="font-size: 17px;">didn't </strong><span style="font-size: 17px;">go into </span><em style="font-size: 17px;">And Ampersand</em><span style="font-size: 17px;">, and what readers can look forward to when they read this collection of short stories.</span></p>
<p><!-- /divi:paragraph -->[/et_pb_text][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][et_pb_row _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”][et_pb_column type=”4_4&#8243; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”][et_pb_button button_url=”<a href="https://www.nedaaria.info/post/writer-vs-writer-interview-ryan-r-campbell&#038;#8221" rel="nofollow">https://www.nedaaria.info/post/writer-vs-writer-interview-ryan-r-campbell&#038;#8221</a>; url_new_window=”on” button_text=”READ THE FULL INTERVIEW HERE” button_alignment=”center” _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” custom_button=”on” button_text_color=”#000000&#8243; button_letter_spacing=”2px” hover_enabled=”0&#8243; button_font=”|600|||||||” sticky_enabled=”0&#8243;][/et_pb_button][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][et_pb_row column_structure=”1_2,1_2&#8243; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” background_color=”rgba(0,0,0,0)” animation_style=”fade” global_module=”9256&#8243;][et_pb_column type=”1_2&#8243; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”][et_pb_image src=”<a href="https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/And-Ampersand-Kindle.png&#038;#8221">https://ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/And-Ampersand-Kindle.png&#038;#8221</a>; title_text=”And Ampersand Kindle” align=”center” _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default” background_color=”rgba(0,0,0,0)” animation_style=”fade”][/et_pb_image][/et_pb_column][et_pb_column type=”1_2&#8243; _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”][et_pb_text _builder_version=”4.7.7&#8243; _module_preset=”default”]</p>
<h2 style="text-align: center;">Preorder Now</h2>
<p style="text-align: center;"><em>And Ampersand: Short Stories on Endings and Beginnings (of a Sort)</em> is available April 12th, 2021.</p>
