<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whatever it means—however it feels—you likely know the feeling, that moment of innocence lost, the sharing of words better left unsaid. These are points of no return, of horrible devastation and insurmountable grief.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But within these moments, at the bottom of the crater they leave behind, cracks begin to form. Water trickles in, pooling, paving the way for life where once there was none. It's glacial, this process, and there are days, weeks, months during which we swear the water has not risen, that the lichen now growing on the crater's sides must have always been present.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
