<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In time, the water's softly lapping waves become alluring. We dip in our toes, but the water proves too cold. We fear we've forgotten how to swim. We fear what lies beneath, for the crater is still there.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But the crater, we must understand, never disappears, not truly. There is no erasing its impact, no denying the ruin it once wrought.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
