      571548442,
    ],
    "comment_status": "open",
    "content": {
      "protected": false,
      "rendered": "<p><span class="embed-youtube" style="text-align:center; display: block;"><iframe loading="lazy" class="youtube-player" width="1080" height="608" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/uYRM0kq61m8?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent" allowfullscreen="true" style="border:0;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox"></iframe></span></p>
<p>As writers, we can get so focused on improving our craft or learning the ins and outs of book marketing that we lose our sense of self. Don't fall for that trap! Take time and make space for the non-writerly parts of you, too; it'll help you feel more refreshed when it's time to return to the page.</p>
<span class="et_bloom_bottom_trigger"></span>",
    },
    "date": "2020-07-07T07:10:30",
    "date_gmt": "2020-07-07T12:10:30",
