    "comment_status": "open",
    "content": {
      "protected": false,
      "rendered": "<p><span class="embed-youtube" style="text-align:center; display: block;"><iframe loading="lazy" class="youtube-player" width="1080" height="608" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/pa7YO83e1WY?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent" allowfullscreen="true" style="border:0;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox"></iframe></span></p>
<p>As a writer, you're a content creator, so if you create it, they'll consume it. Right? Wrong. To reach readers and other writers, you have to do more than broadcast your own content out into the universe; you have to reach others where they're at as well. In this morning's meditation, exploration, and affirmation, we talk about doing just that.</p>
<span class="et_bloom_bottom_trigger"></span>",
    },
