    "episode_featured_image": "/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/RR-Site-Post-Header-Murder-Character-Death-Post-2.png",
    "episode_player_image": "https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/2020-Writescast-Network-Logo.jpg?fit=3000%2C3000&ssl=1",
    "excerpt": {
      "protected": false,
      "rendered": "Kill your darlings, they say. Every writer has at least heard the phrase, and the interpretations of what it really means vary from deleting a favorite phrase to an entire beat or event. Those darlings aren't what we'll focus on in this post, however. Today, we're talking murder&#8212;actual, literary murder. In literature as in life, people die. George […]",
    },
