    "comment_status": "open",
    "content": {
      "protected": false,
      "rendered": "<p style="text-align: center;"><em>This post contains affiliate links. For more information, see my disclosures <a href="http://www.rrcampbellwrites.com/disclosures" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.</em></p>
<p>If you've visited this site or my social media profiles before, you've likely noticed scores of high-quality images of <a href="http://www.rrcampbellwrites.com/books" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">my books</a> in a number of picturesque settings. This might have had you wondering…</p>
<p>Who did r.r. pay to take those photos? How much did he have to fork over? Was what he paid possibly worth it?</p>
<p><strong>I'll let you in on a secret. </strong></p>
<p>I didn't pay a photographer for those photos, and I was able to create them for far less than you might think.</p>
<p>How did I make the amazing photos below? <a href="http://adazing.ontraport.com/t?orid=195960&amp;opid=26" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mockup Shots.</a></p>
