    "comment_status": "open",
    "content": {
      "protected": false,
      "rendered": "<p style="text-align: center;"><em>This is part four of the misadventures of the <a href="http://www.rrcampbellwrites.com/podcasts">Writescast</a> Raconteurs. For more on what this is and why it’s happening, feel free to check out the <a href="https://ryanrcampbell.com/writescast-raconteurs/">Writescast Raconteurs home page</a>.</em></p>
<p>The title says it all. Let's just&#8212;yeah. Here's the scoreboard.</p>
<h1>Scoreboard</h1>
<div id="attachment_4079" style="width: 972px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-4079" data-attachment-id="4079" data-permalink="https://ryanrcampbell.com/screen-shot-2017-09-25-at-7-24-03-pm/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/Screen-Shot-2017-09-25-at-7.24.03-PM.png?fit=962%2C555&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="962,555" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Screen Shot 2017-09-25 at 7.24.03 PM" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/Screen-Shot-2017-09-25-at-7.24.03-PM.png?fit=300%2C173&amp;ssl=1" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/Screen-Shot-2017-09-25-at-7.24.03-PM.png?fit=962%2C555&amp;ssl=1" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-4079" src="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/Screen-Shot-2017-09-25-at-7.24.03-PM.png?resize=962%2C555&#038;ssl=1" alt="Screen Shot 2017-09-25 at 7.24.03 PM" width="962" height="555" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/Screen-Shot-2017-09-25-at-7.24.03-PM.png?w=962&amp;ssl=1 962w, https://i0.wp.com/ryanrcampbell.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/Screen-Shot-2017-09-25-at-7.24.03-PM.png?resize=300%2C173&amp;ssl=1 300w" sizes="(max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px" data-recalc-dims="1" /><p id="caption-attachment-4079" class="wp-caption-text">A failure to execute at all levels.</p></div>
<p>Every part of this week went poorly. The execution was shite from everyone on the squad&#8212;myself included, as I made a number of roster moves and substitutions that left us with far fewer points than could have otherwise been earned.</p>
<p>The good(?) news is that even if I <em>had</em> made the right calls, the team still would have lost by about six points. What I'm trying to say is that for the second week in a row, we had no chance because players on my opponents' teams KEEP POPPING OFF WHEN I PLAY THEM.</p>
<p>Here's what to look forward to in the coming weeks:</p>
<ul>
<li>I will stop panicking and replacing guys who underperform for a single week</li>
</ul>
<p>And that's… I don't know. I think that might be it. Basically, I need to rethink my approach to setting the lineup and playing the waiver wire each week. There's a way forward; I just have to put a little more care into finding it.</p>
<p>Or, you know, I could focus on getting my synopsis together for <em><a href="http://www.rrcampbellwrites.com/current-projects" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Accounting for it All</a></em>, since completing it is the only thing keeping me from having a complete query package put together.</p>
<p>I'll let you guess which priority might win out over the course of the coming weeks. 🙂</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<span class="et_bloom_bottom_trigger"></span>",
